---
id: PY-004
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: 'bare except, or an inline except ...: pass swallow'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 5

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '\bexcept\s*:|\bexcept[^:]*:\s*pass\b'

related: [PY-006, PY-010]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

A bare `except:` (or `except ...: pass`) catches `KeyboardInterrupt`,
`SystemExit`, and ordinary bugs alike, then discards them — the program runs on
in an unknown state and the real fault is invisible. Catch the narrowest
exception you can handle and re-raise or log the rest:
`except ValueError as e: raise ConfigError(...) from e`. If swallowing really is
correct (a top-level daemon guard that logs), suppress with that reason:
`# @anvil-ignore PY-004 -- top-level guard, logs and continues`.

Detection is line-oriented: a bare `except:` and an inline `except ...: pass`
are caught, but a named handler whose `pass` sits on the *next* line
(`except Exception:` then an indented `pass`) is not — that needs block
context this regex tier does not have.
